        # Now for external access (LAN/internet → ns1 service):

            You need port forwarding (DNAT).
            Example the set up is :

                    host Wi-Fi IP: 10.0.0.55
                    ns1 IP: 10.0.1.2
                    service port: 8080

     # Add forwarding rule:

            > iptables -t nat -A PREROUTING -i wlo1 -p tcp --dport 8080 -j DNAT --to-destination 10.0.1.2:8080

     # Allow forwarding:

            > iptables -A FORWARD -p tcp -d 10.0.1.2 --dport 8080 -j ACCEPT

     # Now another machine on your LAN can access:

            http://10.0.0.55:8080
